# Module convention

A module is one screen cluster. Phase 1 names: `home`, `auth`, `catalog`, `play`, `profile`, `news`, `rewards`.

```
src/modules/<name>/
  routes/routes.tsx      # required — default export RouteObject[]
  pages/                 # routed screens
  components/            # UI used only in this module
  hooks/                 # UI hooks (not HTTP clients)
```

```tsx
// src/modules/play/routes/routes.tsx
import { routePaths } from "@/routes/route-path";
import lazyWithPreload from "@/infrastructure/plugins/lazy-preload";

const PlayPage = lazyWithPreload(() => import("../pages/PlayPage"));

export default [
  { path: routePaths.play, element: <PlayPage /> },
];
```

- Keep pages thin: read context and call `useXxxQueries` / `useXxxMutations` from `@/domain/services/...`.
- Do not add `services/` or `api.ts` inside a module.
- If a component is reused by another module, move it to `src/shared-components/`.
- Mobile-first. The play page only embeds the game and shows coin balance. Game rules stay inside the game.
- Comments in this folder are English. UI strings go through i18n.
